  "worked_solution": "In part 6, we found that the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\nm=2.\n$$\n\nTo find the equation of the tangent, we use the point-slope form with the coordinates of $A$ and $m.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(1) & =(2)(x-0) \\\\ y-1 & =2x \\\\ y & =2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
